<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Open watchdog preset from Cfg_OpenTime (ms). Only loaded if > 0, otherwise the 5000 ms default is kept.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(Cfg_OpenTime,0)MOV(Cfg_OpenTime,OpenWD.PRE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Close watchdog preset from Cfg_CloseTime (ms). Only loaded if > 0, otherwise the 5000 ms default is kept.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(Cfg_CloseTime,0)MOV(Cfg_CloseTime,CloseWD.PRE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Open solenoid - on only while Cmd_Open is held. When off, the spring closes the valve.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cmd_Open)OTE(Out_OpenSol);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Confirmed open: open prox on, closed prox off.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_OpenedPrx)XIO(Inp_ClosedPrx)OTE(Sts_Opened);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Confirmed closed: closed prox on, open prox off.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_ClosedPrx)XIO(Inp_OpenedPrx)OTE(Sts_Closed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Prox fault: both proxes on at the same time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_OpenedPrx)XIC(Inp_ClosedPrx)OTE(Sts_ProxFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Opening: open solenoid on and not yet confirmed open.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Out_OpenSol)XIO(Sts_Opened)OTE(Sts_Opening);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Closing: open solenoid off (spring closing) and not yet confirmed closed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Out_OpenSol)XIO(Sts_Closed)OTE(Sts_Closing);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Open watchdog: times while opening, resets when open prox is made or the request drops.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Opening)TON(OpenWD,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Close watchdog: times while spring closing, resets when closed prox is made or the open request comes back on.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Closing)TON(CloseWD,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Open fault: watchdog timed out.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OpenWD.DN)OTE(Sts_OpenFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Close fault: watchdog timed out.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(CloseWD.DN)OTE(Sts_CloseFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Digital alarm - failed to open. Alarm tag must be configured as Latched; Inp_ProgReset clears it once the fault is gone.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_OpenFault)ALMD(Alm_OpenFail,0,Inp_ProgReset,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Digital alarm - failed to close. Alarm tag must be configured as Latched; Inp_ProgReset clears it once the fault is gone.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_CloseFault)ALMD(Alm_CloseFail,0,Inp_ProgReset,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[OPEN STROKE TIME: Reset the stroke timer whenever the open solenoid is off, ready for the next open.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Out_OpenSol)RES(OpenStroke);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stroke timer accumulates while opening. Being an RTO, it holds its value once the opened prox is made.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Opening)RTO(OpenStroke,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Record the open time once per move (OpenLogged is from the previous scan, so this rung is true for one scan). Shift the array down (oldest in [4] dropped), store newest in [0], output it as Sts_OpenLast, and count samples up to 5.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Out_OpenSol)XIC(Sts_Opened)XIO(OpenLogged)GRT(OpenStroke.ACC,0)[MOV(OpenTimes[3],OpenTimes[4])MOV(OpenTimes[2],OpenTimes[3])MOV(OpenTimes[1],OpenTimes[2])MOV(OpenTimes[0],OpenTimes[1])MOV(OpenStroke.ACC,OpenTimes[0])MOV(OpenStroke.ACC,Sts_OpenLast) ,LES(OpenCount,5)ADD(OpenCount,1,OpenCount) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Seal-in: OpenLogged turns on once opened and stays on while the open solenoid is on, so each move is recorded only once.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Out_OpenSol)[XIC(Sts_Opened) ,XIC(OpenLogged) ]OTE(OpenLogged);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Average open time (ms) = sum of the array / number of samples recorded.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(OpenCount,0)ADD(OpenTimes[0],OpenTimes[1],OpenSum)ADD(OpenSum,OpenTimes[2],OpenSum)ADD(OpenSum,OpenTimes[3],OpenSum)ADD(OpenSum,OpenTimes[4],OpenSum)DIV(OpenSum,OpenCount,Sts_OpenAvg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[CLOSE STROKE TIME: Reset the stroke timer whenever the open solenoid is on, ready for the next close.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Out_OpenSol)RES(CloseStroke);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stroke timer accumulates while closing. Being an RTO, it holds its value once the closed prox is made.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Closing)RTO(CloseStroke,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Record the close time once per move (CloseLogged is from the previous scan, so this rung is true for one scan). Shift the array down (oldest in [4] dropped), store newest in [0], output it as Sts_CloseLast, and count samples up to 5.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Out_OpenSol)XIC(Sts_Closed)XIO(CloseLogged)GRT(CloseStroke.ACC,0)[MOV(CloseTimes[3],CloseTimes[4])MOV(CloseTimes[2],CloseTimes[3])MOV(CloseTimes[1],CloseTimes[2])MOV(CloseTimes[0],CloseTimes[1])MOV(CloseStroke.ACC,CloseTimes[0])MOV(CloseStroke.ACC,Sts_CloseLast) ,LES(CloseCount,5)ADD(CloseCount,1,CloseCount) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Seal-in: CloseLogged turns on once closed and stays on while the open solenoid is off, so each move is recorded only once.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Out_OpenSol)[XIC(Sts_Closed) ,XIC(CloseLogged) ]OTE(CloseLogged);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Average close time (ms) = sum of the array / number of samples recorded.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(CloseCount,0)ADD(CloseTimes[0],CloseTimes[1],CloseSum)ADD(CloseSum,CloseTimes[2],CloseSum)ADD(CloseSum,CloseTimes[3],CloseSum)ADD(CloseSum,CloseTimes[4],CloseSum)DIV(CloseSum,CloseCount,Sts_CloseAvg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[ANGLE CHECK: Delay preset from Cfg_AngleDelay (ms). Only loaded if > 0, otherwise the 60000 ms default is kept.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GRT(Cfg_AngleDelay,0)MOV(Cfg_AngleDelay,AngleDelayTmr.PRE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Live deviation from the installed closed angle, and the high/low limits (closed angle +/- allowed deviation).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SUB(Inp_Angle,Cfg_ClosedAngle,Sts_AngleDeviation)ADD(Cfg_ClosedAngle,Cfg_AngleDev,AngleHiLimit)SUB(Cfg_ClosedAngle,Cfg_AngleDev,AngleLoLimit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Delay timer runs while the valve is confirmed closed. Resets as soon as it leaves the closed position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Closed)TON(AngleDelayTmr,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Angle high: closed for the delay time and angle is above the high limit.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AngleDelayTmr.DN)GRT(Inp_Angle,AngleHiLimit)OTE(Sts_AngleHigh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Angle low: closed for the delay time and angle is below the low limit.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(AngleDelayTmr.DN)LES(Inp_Angle,AngleLoLimit)OTE(Sts_AngleLow);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Angle fault: either high or low.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_AngleHigh) ,XIC(Sts_AngleLow) ]OTE(Sts_AngleFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Digital alarm - closed angle out of tolerance. Alarm tag must be configured as Latched; Inp_ProgReset clears it once the fault is gone.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_AngleFault)ALMD(Alm_AngleDev,0,Inp_ProgReset,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
